# CODEOWNERS — CS-1R4: independent review for the WHOLE root-of-trust.
#
# WHY. The CS-1 integrity gates prove fiscal-neutrality by comparing against PINNED
# data (fingerprints, approved blob SHAs, a graph closure lock, inventory manifests)
# AND by an UNCONDITIONAL required CI job (rust-prro.yml) that runs build+test for
# every workspace member. That trust chain is only as strong as its weakest
# un-reviewed link. CS-1R4 moved the trust boundary OUT of PR-code and INTO merge
# rules: the CODE is fail-closed and un-dispatchable, and every file that DEFINES the
# gate — the workflows, the oracles/engines, the pins, the inventory, the toolchain
# pin, the .sqlx describe cache, and this file — is code-owner-gated so weakening any
# of them is a reviewed, owner-gated event, never a silent self-edit.
#
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# OPERATOR ACTION REQUIRED (cannot be set from code — the ACTUAL trust root):
#   1. Enable branch protection on `main`:  Settings → Branches → main →
#      "Require a pull request before merging" → "Require review from Code Owners"
#      AND "Require status checks to pass" with the REQUIRED contexts:
#        - x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu   (rust-prro.yml — the integrity job)
#        - fmt + clippy (gnu)         (fmt-clippy.yml)
#        - mutation diff-gate         (mutation-diff.yml)
#      Also enable "Do not allow bypassing the above settings" and disallow force-push.
#      Without these flags, CODEOWNERS + the required jobs are ADVISORY only:
#        - a skipped/green-without-running required check counts as satisfied;
#        - self-disabling a workflow (e.g. deleting a step, `if: false`) is a
#          workflow-file diff that ONLY the CODEOWNERS + required-review rule gates.
#      THE CODE CANNOT enforce these — they are the trust root and live in repo rules.
#   2. Set an INDEPENDENT owner. GitHub does NOT count the PR author as a satisfying
#      code-owner reviewer, so `@Setter1981` below already forces a second party for
#      any PR that party did not author. For genuine two-person integrity on
#      solo-authored PRs, add a second maintainer or a review team here (e.g.
#      `@your-org/cs1r-gate-reviewers`) and require it.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── CI workflows — the required-job DEFINITIONS (the structural gate surface). ──
# A change that weakens a required job (removes a step, adds `if:`/`continue-on-error`,
# changes a `checkout` ref, un-pins an action, drops `--locked`) is owner-reviewed.
/.github/workflows/**                           @Setter1981

# ── The CS-1 test-provenance gate — oracle + engine + the coverage assertion. ──
/rust/prro/tests/cs1_test_provenance.rs         @Setter1981
/rust/prro/tests/support/cs1_provenance.rs      @Setter1981
/rust/prro/tests/cs1r4_integrity_job_coverage.rs @Setter1981

# ── prro-domain purity gate — oracle + engine + the committed closure lock. ──
/rust/prro-domain/tests/purity_gate.rs          @Setter1981
/rust/prro-domain/tests/support/metadata_graph.rs @Setter1981
/rust/prro-domain/purity-closure.lock           @Setter1981

# ── CS-1R docs, pins, and inventory (the whole docs/cs1r surface). ──
# Covers the pins the gates LOAD, the forward inventory baseline, and the honest
# artifact/claim docs. `/docs/cs1r/**` subsumes pins/ and inventory/.
/docs/cs1r/**                                   @Setter1981

# ── CS-1R gate scripts (the inventory gate + mint + this surface). ──
/scripts/cs1r/**                                @Setter1981

# ── The toolchain pin (channel/components/targets the whole gate builds under). ──
/rust/rust-toolchain.toml                       @Setter1981

# ── The committed sqlx describe cache (the offline SQL the build resolves against;
#    a change here changes what SQL the gates compile without a live DB). ──
/rust/**/.sqlx/**                               @Setter1981

# ── This ownership file itself (a change to who reviews the gates is itself gated). ──
/.github/CODEOWNERS                             @Setter1981
